# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .gitignore — SPX Diagonal Calendar Analyzer
#
# NOTE ON ENCODING: this file must be saved as UTF-8 with LF line endings.
# The previous version was corrupted by PowerShell's Add-Content/Out-File,
# which default to UTF-16LE; the appended null-separated bytes matched nothing,
# so the intended `pinned_pairs.json` entry was silently inert.
# If you must append from PowerShell, use:  Add-Content -Encoding utf8
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets & credentials — NEVER commit ─────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/token.json
*token*.json
# Anything with "token" in the name, whatever the extension. The narrower
# `*token*.json` above missed `token.json.bak-20260802-063131` — a real file
# found untracked on 2026-08-09, one careless `git add .` from being published.
# A dated suffix is exactly what a re-auth backup looks like.
*token*

# ── Recorded output of the briefing daemon ───────────────────────────────────
# The forecast log is a RUNTIME RECORD, not source: the daemon appends to it
# about fifteen times a trading day, and `scripts/score_briefings.py` reads it
# back to grade what the model predicted. Committing it would put a churning
# data file in every diff and would mean a pull could silently overwrite the
# only copy of a day's forecasts. Same posture as the database above — `data/`
# holds a `.gitkeep` and nothing else, and this keeps it that way.
data/*.jsonl
# Backups taken before a trim or a rewrite. Never wanted in the history.
*.pre-trim

# ── Databases (irreplaceable market data; backed up out-of-tree) ─────────────
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Dated/suffixed database backups — dashboard.db.2026-08-19, .bak, etc.
# `*.db` alone does not match these: the suffix comes AFTER the extension,
# and a 2.7 GB file staged by accident is not something to notice late.
*.db.*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ── Runtime / machine-generated state ────────────────────────────────────────
# Live application state, not source. These churn on every run and make
# `git log -p` unusable for code archaeology when tracked.
eligible_history.json
entry_locks.json
chart_colors.json
pinned_pairs.json
# The watchdog's "have I already complained about this?" note (M3.4).
watchdog_state.json

# Single-instance lock held by the running collector (see collector.py).
.collector.lock

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
# Rotated logs: collector.log.1, collector.log.2026-08-09, etc. `*.log` alone
# does not match these — the suffix comes after.
*.log.*
logs/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Tooling caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/

# ── Editors & OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Streamlit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .streamlit/config.toml IS tracked (it carries the dark theme); secrets are not.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# ── Local scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*_backup.py
*.bak
scratch/

# ── Frontend (M6, React + Vite under web/) ───────────────────────────────────
# node_modules is ~200 MB of reinstallable dependencies pinned by
# package-lock.json, which IS committed. dist/ is build output.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
